> be a pain to eliminate, but we should add that sort of thing to the
> list of sources of suboptimal efficiency.

We should be recalculating log(sigma_alpha) and log(sigma_beta)
in each loop for n in 1:N.  And additionally log(sigma_y) for
each n in 1:N and each t in 1:T.

   for (n in 1:N) {
     alpha[n] ~ normal(mu_alpha, sigma_alpha);
     beta[n] ~ normal(mu_beta, sigma_beta);

     for (t in 1:T)

       y[n,t] ~ normal(alpha[n] + beta[n] * (x[t] - xbar), sigma_y);
   }

I just realized from your comment that we could compute these
once and reuse the computations in the loop.   That, I don't know
how to automate.

