PPS: There was a bug in the way I was learning the rescaling parameters for NUTS before, which is why it wasn't helping. When you do it right, it totally works, unsurprisingly. But it can get into big trouble if you start rescaling during burn-in, since the "standard deviations" are actually just a measure of how badly you initialized the parameters and don't relate at all to the proper scale. This could be fixed by 1. doing a better job of initializing, e.g. using an optimizer or 2. something else, like maybe estimating the standard deviations using mini batches that throw away previous mini batches completely.

