When I wrote the original R-hat function, it had an option to specify varaibles to be transformed as log or logit, and that's what I've done in my applications.  But it's not a really big deal.  If we want to be consistent with Jags we can monitor on the original scale.  We also have nonparametric versions of R-hat and ESS but, as you keep reminding us, these are more difficult to compute!

